ge's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine start_timer ( title ) character ( len =* ), optional :: title if ( present ( title )) write ( * , \"(A)\" ) trim ( title ) // \":\" timer_index = timer_index + 1 if ( timer_index > size ( timer_start , 1 )) then stop \"Error in cronograph: too many timers started\" endif call date_and_time ( values = timer_start ( timer_index ,:)) timer0 ( timer_index ,:) = timer_start ( timer_index ,:) !init variables for ETA: elapsed_time = 0.0 old_time = 0.0 time = 0.0 ! end subroutine start_timer","tags":"","url":"proc/start_timer.html"},{"title":"start_progress – SciFortran","text":"public  subroutine start_progress(unit) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, optional :: unit Calls proc~~start_progress~~CallsGraph proc~start_progress start_progress proc~start_timer start_timer proc~start_progress->proc~start_timer Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine start_progress ( unit ) integer , optional :: unit funit = 6 ; if ( present ( unit )) funit = unit !open(funit,carriagecontrol='fortran') open ( funit ) call start_timer end subroutine start_progress","tags":"","url":"proc/start_progress.html"},{"title":"stop_timer – SciFortran","text":"public  subroutine stop_timer(title, unit) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), optional :: title integer, optional :: unit Called by proc~~stop_timer~~CalledByGraph proc~stop_timer stop_timer proc~stop_progress stop_progress proc~stop_progress->proc~stop_timer Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine stop_timer ( title , unit ) character ( len =* ), optional :: title integer , optional :: unit integer :: unit_ integer , dimension ( 8 ) :: itimer unit_ = 6 ; if ( present ( unit )) unit_ = unit call date_and_time ( values = timer_stop ( timer_index ,:)) itimer = time_difference ( timer_stop ( timer_index ,:), timer_start ( timer_index ,:)) if ( present ( title )) then call print_total_time ( itimer , unit , title ) else call print_total_time ( itimer , unit ) endif timer_start ( timer_index ,:) = 0 timer_stop ( timer_index ,:) = 0 if ( timer_index > 1 ) then timer_index = timer_index - 1 else timer_index = 0 endif end subroutine stop_timer","tags":"","url":"proc/stop_timer.html"},{"title":"stop_progress – SciFortran","text":"public  subroutine stop_progress() Arguments None Calls proc~~stop_progress~~CallsGraph proc~stop_progress stop_progress proc~stop_timer stop_timer proc~stop_progress->proc~stop_timer Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure